# {{ .name }}

Shared contracts class library for the integration system. Sibling components
reference it via `ProjectReference` and exchange these contract types over
pub/sub — the extractor publishes `{{ .contract }}`, the consuming loader deserializes
the same record.

This project was scaffolded automatically as a dependency of the first
component that needed it. Rendering further components into the same parent
directory leaves it untouched.

{{- if and (hasKey . "messages") .messages }}

## Generated contracts

These contract types are generated from the payload schemas the registry
pins, not written by hand. The schema documents are committed under
`schemas/`, and `.intropy/messages.json` records which message each one
belongs to.

Run these from this directory — the paths are relative to it.

{{ range .messages }}`{{ .contract }}` carries `{{ .message }}`. Generate it with:

```bash
npx --yes quicktype@23 --src-lang schema --lang csharp \
  --framework SystemTextJson --namespace {{ $.name }} \
  --top-level {{ .contract }} \
  -o {{ .contract }}.cs {{ .schemaFile }}
```

{{ end }}Then:

```bash
dotnet build
```

**The project does not compile until you run it.** That is deliberate: an
empty placeholder record would compile and then silently drop every payload
at run time, which is far harder to notice than a build error.

Re-run the same command after a pin moves. The generator reads the committed
document, so it never contacts the registry.

The generator and its flags are the template library's choice, and
`ContractOptions.cs` is the single seam components and the framework use to
reach its serialization settings. Change both there to change how types are
produced.
{{- if gt (len .messages) 1 }}

> **This preview supports one generated contract per project, and this one
> has {{ len .messages }}.** The generator emits its own helper classes into
> every file it writes, so a second contract in the same namespace collides
> at build time (`CS0101`). Generate one and write the others by hand until
> per-message namespaces land.
